# Paisa - AI provider credentials.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE key. .env is gitignored; this example
# is not, so never put a real key in this file.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# A variable already set in your real environment wins over anything here, so a
# CI secret is not shadowed by a stale .env in a checkout.
#
# Only the model layer (L3) uses these. L0-L2 and `--no-llm` need no credentials
# at all, and with no key set the pipeline runs on a stub provider that cannot
# produce a match.


# --- Pick one ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Auto-detection checks these in exactly this order and uses the first one set.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# Ollama needs no key. If nothing above is set, auto-detection probes for a
# local Ollama before falling back to the stub.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434


# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Force a provider regardless of which keys are present. A --provider flag on
# the command line still overrides this.
# Valid: openai | anthropic | gemini | groq | ollama | dummy
# PAISA_AI_PROVIDER=openai
